  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\n   The central idea is to use a periodic structure inspired by the derived function f(x) = 0.5 + 0.25*sin(\u03c0*x) but normalized and scaled to fit the domain [0,2]. The function is chosen because it inherently balances the distribution of h(x) and 1-h(x) to minimize peak overlaps. The rationale is that this geometric form reduces the maximum correlation across shifts by distributing peaks and valleys more evenly, which the previous algorithm struggled with by getting trapped in local extima.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\n   Define the periodic signal with period 2:\n      g(x) = 0.5 + 0.25*sin(\u03c0*x) + 0.25*sin(3*\u03c0*x)  [3-term Fourier approximation]\n   Normalize g(x) to satisfy the integral constraint:\n      Integral_{0}^{2} g(x) dx = 1\n   For discretization:\n      h_values = g(x) interpolated onto [0,2] at 700 points\n      Enforce constraints: 0 <= h_val <= 1 and sum(h) = 350 (for n=700)\n   The objective is: \n      C_5 = max_k integral h(x)*(1-h(x+k)) dx\n   The continuous sinusoidal form will be approximated and slightly modified to avoid boundary issues, then projected to satisfy constraints.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\n   - Validate input n_points: prefer 700 if `initial_h_values` provided\n   - Compute initial_h_values as normalized Fourier series\n      Let x = np.linspace(0,2, n_points)\n      g = 0.5 + 0.25*np.sin(np.pi*x) + 0.25*np.sin(3*np.pi*x)\n      Clip and rescale g to [0,1] while maintaining integral 1\n   - Use coordinate descent for local refinement:\n        - Start with initial_h_values from above\n        - Apply projected gradient steps for maxiter=1000\n        - Use random m=50 restarts with clipped Gaussian initialization\n   - Stop early and report best candidate every 100 seconds\n   - Back-transform n-differences to parent space with valid interpolation\n   - Preserve feasibility and recompute C_5 using dx=2/n\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations:\n   - Fourier basis: 3 terms (adjustable), use parent if available\n   - Local optimizer: Projected gradient descent (\u03b1=0.05-0.1)\n   - Random restarts: 50 total, vary initial distribution width (0.01 to 0.05)\n   - Project Feasible: After optimization, force sum(h)=350\n\n5. Computer Budget and Robustness:\n   - Time: 1100s budget, check for deadlines every 500 iterations\n   - Memory: Traverse n_dimensions=700 (minor cost)\n   - Projection: Explicit validation and feasibility repair\n   - High-dimensional projections handled by diffusion interpolation\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\n   - Check: 0<=h<1, sum(h)==n/2 (project if needed)\n   - Re-evaluate: Use same max_convolution method\n   - Final check: Minimize C_5 without losing parent validity\n   - For invalid candidates, fall back to initial_h_values",
